Pure and simple, this is just great writing and that was the point when I realized -

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:25.280
Holy crap! This series might actually be something really special.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:29.580
Hopefully you're getting the idea by now that every arc so far has taken what's been previously established

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:35.840
and added something new and built upon that foundation, but that doesn't really happen in the next arc.

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:38.940
Because it kind of just does everything at ones.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:42.860
OST Attack on Titan Season 3 OST -  Apple Seed by Hiroyuki Sawano ft. Laco &amp; Mpi

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:49.480
Remember when Attack on Titan was about Titans?

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:51.980
Remember when it was about humanity taking back the walls?

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:55.620
Remember when it was about getting to Eren's basement ?

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.000
Here you go. Are you happy now?

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.520
Are you happy? Are you finally gonna shut the fuck up?

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:04.280
Attack on Titan Season 3 Part 2, god that name never rolls off the tongue no matter how many times I say it.

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:06.680
It's a combination of everything the series has built up.

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:11.940
Its the action-packed rollercoaster of the first season with the weight of the second, the emotional complexity of the third

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:15.020
and holy fuck, is it an amazing sight to behold.

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:19.360
You may not like it, but this is what peak Attack on Titan looks like.

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:23.600
It's like the series is going through a greatest hits compilation of everything it was able to achieve

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:27.980
where the final product is even better than all the individual elements it added.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:33.420
You've still got the amazingly directed action sequences, the epic reveal of the world and the mysteries build-up,

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:41.300
really difficult character decisions, consequence to every action and all this equates to an experience you can rarely find in anime.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:48.980
I really hate how cliche the term Edge-of-your-seat has become because this is truly edge-of-your-seat stuff.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:52.840
But I don't feel that term is justice to convey just how well it's built up its characters

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:56.920
and stakes so you go to every episode with a mix of fear, excitement and anticipation

00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:01.380
because you genuinely do not know what is going to happen.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:05.140
You watch with bated breath knowing not everyone is going to make it out of this.

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:09.000
It's not a matter of if, it's a matter of who, when and how many.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:14.580
And now that we've reached a point where you actually care about these characters and it's not fucking two-lined Lenny riding to his death.

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:20.880
Every event whether that be a small victory in battle or someone's unfortunate demise has tremendous weight behind it.

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:24.060
Side characters no longer feel like side characters.

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:27.780
Most of them now you've gotten to know for a decent amount of time with meaningful development.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.560
And I'm not talking about something like -

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:40.080
That's some premium character development right there!

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:44.180
You're invested, you're hopeful, you've gone through this long arduous journey with them

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:47.920
and seeing everyone playing this giant game of russian roulette every episode,

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:54.300
brings the same kind of squeaky bum, gut-wrenching tension as when it's the 90th minute in the World Cup final, it's stoppage time

00:18:54.309 --> 00:18:59.360
and your team is one goal away from winning or losing the entire tournament.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:01.989
Except this isn't some live sporting event,

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:03.760
It's a premade animation.

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:09.360
It brings an emotional weight that has never been reached before by this show and is rarely reached by any show.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:14.480
And none of this would have been possible without the way it's constantly evolved and build-up upon itself.

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:20.420
Essentially, the series itself went on this 26 episode hyperbolic time chamber training arc,

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:24.300
level up every aspect to continue its journey stronger than ever.

00:19:24.309 --> 00:19:29.589
So now I hope you understand why I've needed to spend 19 minutes of your time going through every season,

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:32.340
explaining what's all the individual seasons have done

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:38.320
and that's because where we are at right now would not be possible without the combined effort of every season.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:46.940
And now that we're at this point looking back at season 1, there were a lot of elements, I wasn't too fond of back then that now I'm glad they did.

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:49.120
I'm glad people can change into Titans.

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:51.940
I'm glad they didn't just take the wall back straight away.

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:58.460
I'm glad they took the time to introduce the female Titan and this mysterious external entity who wants to destroy humanity.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:03.060
I'm glad they didn't just stay on that simple rollercoaster and stick to humans versus mindless titans

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:09.760
because now the story is far more intricate and diverse than anything I had predicted when I first started watching it.

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:13.800
After this latest reveal of what's in the basement and the secrets of the world have been unpacked,

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:17.240
once again the show has evolved into something entirely new.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:19.780
It doesn't even feel like the same show anymore.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.500
And I mean that in a good way.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:26.660
It's resulted in a far more interesting world with a richer history than I ever thought it was going to be

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.980
while still sticking to the same themes presented in Episode 1.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:35.360
And through me realizing this I've just come to appreciate how rare and enigma of this show has become.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:40.340
Because it's one that has been fully able to realize its potential until the very end.

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:44.340
How many of you have had an anime you like so you go off to read the source material,

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:47.140
only to find that the anime barely scratched the surface

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:51.900
And the source material reaches heights you can only dream of seeing in the anime.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:55.440
Well, Attack on Titan, is that one in a million adaptation.

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:59.520
Not just a really good short hard-hitting series that said its piece and ended

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:06.660
but a full epic that we've gone on this long ride with and has been able to hit its final form with no compromise.

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:12.200
In the process of making this video Season 4 was announced which is going to be the final season.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:17.920
We are going to see a conclusion to this story and if word of mouth of every manga reader I've talked to is true,

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:22.340
things are going to get even better which considering how things have been set up now,

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:24.260
I absolutely believe.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:30.520
So here I am now, in 2019, unironically telling you that you should watch Attack on Titan.

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:35.100
Whether you're a new fan, or old one or even someone who wasn't too hot on season 1

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:42.120
because when I say I like Attack on Titan, a lot of people still associate it with that one dimensional rollercoaster season 1 was.

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:44.580
And it's just so much more than that now.

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:46.360
Believe the hype.

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:47.780
Believe the anticipation.

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:51.840
Forget what I said about The Death of Classic Anime because when this ends

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:58.260
if by some miracle it is able to continue to get the same amazing treatment this adaptation has received thus far -

00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:03.520
This could very much be THE anime that defines this generation...

